.TP
.B free
Print one report in kibibytes (the default unit) and exit.
.TP
.B free \-h
Use human-readable units (Ki, Mi, Gi, …). Combine with \fB\-\-si\fR to
use SI suffixes (K, M, G, …) and powers of 1000.
.TP
.B free \-m
Display values in mebibytes. \fB\-\-mega\fR uses powers of 1000 instead
(megabytes).
.TP
.B free \-s 1
Refresh once per second until interrupted. Combine with \fB\-c N\fR to
repeat exactly \fIN\fR times.
.TP
.B free \-w
Wide mode: split the \fIBUFF/CACHE\fR column into separate \fIbuffers\fR
and \fIcache\fR columns.
.TP
.B free \-L
Single-line output with labelled \fBSwapUse\fR, \fBCachUse\fR,
\fBMemUse\fR, and \fBMemFree\fR values.
.TP
.B free \-t
Add a Total row summing physical memory and swap.
.TP
.B free \-v
Append a Comm row showing the kernel's commit limit and currently
committed memory (\fBCommitLimit\fR and \fBCommitted_AS\fR).
